    <div class="subtab-panel" data-subpanel="profile-items">
      <p class="sub"><span id="profile-item-concentration"></span></p>
      <div id="profile-item-table"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="subtab-panel" data-subpanel="profile-ability" hidden>
      <p class="sub"><span id="profile-ability-concentration"></span></p>
      <div id="profile-ability-table"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="subtab-panel" data-subpanel="profile-moves" hidden>
      <div id="profile-move-table"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="subtab-panel" data-subpanel="profile-team-cores" hidden>
      <p class="lead">Which Pokémon most often share a team with this one.</p>
      <details class="method"><summary>How this is computed</summary>
        <p><strong>Co-occurrence</strong> is the raw pairing rate, which mostly re-ranks whoever is individually popular. <strong>Synergy</strong> ranks by lift: how much more often the pair appears together than their individual popularity alone predicts (&times;1.0 is exactly chance). Synergy only counts pairs seen on at least 5 real teams, since lift is noisy below that.</p>
      </details>
      <div class="controls">
        <label>Core size
          <select id="profile-team-core-size">
            <option value="pairs">Pairs</option>
            <option value="triples">Triples</option>
          </select>
        </label>
        <label>Ranked by
          <select id="profile-team-core-metric">
            <option value="synergy">Synergy (lift)</option>
            <option value="co_occurrence">Co-occurrence</option>
          </select>
        </label>
      </div>
      <div id="profile-pair-table"></div>
      <div id="profile-triple-table" hidden></div>
    </div>

    <div class="subtab-panel" data-subpanel="profile-teams" hidden>
      <p class="lead" id="profile-teams-note">The top-placing teams in this regulation that brought this Pokémon.</p>
      <div class="team-card-grid" id="profile-teams"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="subtab-panel" data-subpanel="profile-pressure" hidden>
      <p class="lead">How hard the regulation's attacks hit this Pokémon, by type.</p>
      <details class="method"><summary>How this is computed</summary>
        <p>Each attacking type is weighted by how often the regulation's teams use damaging moves of that type: a Pokémon's usage share times each damaging move's share of its moveset. The multiplier is the standard type chart against this Pokémon's types. This is type-based, not battle results: it ignores abilities, items, Tera-less STAB and who actually brings what into which game.</p>
      </details>
      <p class="pressure-summary" id="profile-pressure-summary"></p>
      <div id="profile-pressure-table"></div>
    </div>

    {# The ladder lens on the profile (docs/upgrade-plan-2027q2.md, S2,
       D3), filled by static/ladder.js. Both panels are Showdown ladder
       data and say so in their chip. #}
    <div class="subtab-panel" data-subpanel="profile-counters" hidden>
      <p class="source-chip-row"><span class="source-chip">Showdown ladder, from battle logs</span></p>
      <p class="lead">The opponents that most often KO this Pokémon or force it out.</p>
      <details class="method"><summary>How this is computed</summary>
        <p>Smogon reads every rated ladder battle in the regulation's month. Each time this Pokémon and an opponent were both in and one of them was KO'd or switched out, that counts as an encounter; the rate is how often it was this Pokémon. Opponents are ranked as Smogon ranks them, by the rate less four standard deviations, so a rate seen in few encounters ranks lower. Only opponents met at least 100 times are listed.</p>
        <p>This is the only Pokémon-vs-Pokémon signal on the site, and it is ladder data from all ratings: Smogon lists a pair only above about 20 encounters, and weighted toward 1760+ players almost none clear that. Tournament results are team vs team.</p>
      </details>
      <p class="sub" id="profile-counters-note"></p>
      <ol class="counter-list" id="profile-counters"></ol>
      <button type="button" class="show-all-btn" id="profile-counters-more" hidden>Show all</button>
    </div>

    <div class="subtab-panel" data-subpanel="profile-spreads" hidden>
      <p class="source-chip-row"><span class="source-chip">Showdown ladder; tournament sheets don't publish spreads</span></p>
      <p class="lead">The Stat Point spreads 1760+ ladder players ran most.</p>
      <p class="sub" id="profile-spreads-note"></p>
      <div id="profile-spreads"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tab-panel" data-panel="archetypes" data-section="teams" hidden>
    <h2 class="panel-title">Detected Archetypes</h2>
    <div data-official-only="Archetypes are detected from official events' teams only." hidden></div>
    <p class="lead">Experimental team identities, each anchored by a three-Pokémon core that recurs across events.</p>
    <details class="method"><summary>How this is computed</summary>
      <p>Qualifying cores appear on at least five teams and have above-chance three-way and average pair lift. Cores sharing two members consolidate under their strongest neighbour; each team gets one primary assignment and may keep one near-tied secondary one.</p>
      <p>The names are neutral on purpose: composition alone does not prove an editorial label such as “Rain” or “Balance.”</p>
    </details>
    <div class="grid-6xn" id="detected-archetype-grid"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="tab-panel" data-panel="speed-tiers" data-section="meta" hidden>
