  <section class="tab-panel" data-panel="matchup" data-section="pokemon" hidden>
    <h2 class="panel-title">Matchup</h2>
    <p class="lead">A damage estimate, type effectiveness and real head-to-head records for two Pokémon.</p>
    {# Official-only views say so on an Online or All scope
       (docs/upgrade-plan-2027q2.md, S1); static/app.js fills these. #}
    <div data-official-only="Head-to-head records cover official events only." hidden></div>
    <details class="method"><summary>How this is computed</summary>
      <p>The calculator assumes level 50 with full investment, 32 Stat Points, in the attacking and defending stat (tournament team sheets publish no Stat Points). It models STAB, type effectiveness, stat stages, weather and the listed items and abilities. It does not model burns, critical hits, multi-hit moves or other items and abilities.</p>
      <p>Head-to-head is measured <strong>team vs team</strong>: no source publishes which Pokémon were brought to a given match.</p>
    </details>
    {# "vs the meta" (docs/upgrade-plan-2027q1.md, P3): one attacker and move
       against the regulation's 12 most-used Pokémon. #}
    <div class="calc-mode" role="group" aria-label="Calculator mode">
      <button type="button" class="calc-mode-btn" data-calc-mode="single" aria-pressed="true">One defender</button>
      <button type="button" class="calc-mode-btn" data-calc-mode="meta" aria-pressed="false">Top 12 of the meta</button>
    </div>
    <div class="matchup-picker-grid" id="matchup-pickers">
      <div class="matchup-side">
        <h4>Attacker</h4>
        <label>Pokémon <select id="matchup-attacker-select"></select></label>
        <div id="matchup-attacker-type" class="type-badge-row"></div>
        <div id="matchup-attacker-stats" class="desc-text"></div>
        <label>Move <select id="matchup-move-select"></select></label>
        <div id="matchup-move-desc" class="desc-text"></div>
        <h4>Setup</h4>
        <div id="matchup-attacker-stages"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="matchup-side" id="matchup-defender-side">
        <h4>Defender</h4>
        <label>Pokémon <select id="matchup-defender-select"></select></label>
        <div id="matchup-defender-type" class="type-badge-row"></div>
        <div id="matchup-defender-stats" class="desc-text"></div>
        <h4>Setup</h4>
        <div id="matchup-defender-stages"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="controls">
      <label>Weather
        <select id="matchup-weather">
          <option value="">None</option>
          <option value="rain">Rain</option>
          <option value="sun">Harsh Sunlight</option>
          <option value="sand">Sandstorm</option>
          <option value="snow">Snow</option>
        </select>
      </label>
    </div>
    <div class="toggle-chip-row" id="matchup-toggle-row"></div>
    <p class="sub" id="matchup-preset-note"></p>
    <div class="damage-result" id="matchup-damage-result"></div>
    <div id="matchup-meta" hidden>
      <p class="sub">Estimated damage from the attacker's move against the 12 most-used Pokémon in the regulation, each with its own #1 set's Intimidate where it has one. An estimate: level 50 and full investment (32 Stat Points) in the attacking and defending stats, since team sheets publish no Stat Points.</p>
      <div id="matchup-meta-table"></div>
    </div>

    <h3>Type effectiveness</h3>
    <p class="sub">The attacker's type(s) against the defender's type(s).</p>
    <div class="type-effect-grid" id="matchup-type-grid"></div>

    <h3>Head-to-head record</h3>
    <p class="sub">
      How often teams fielding the attacker actually beat teams fielding the
      defender, from real tournament pairings. Ranked by a 95% Wilson lower
      bound, so a 1&#8209;0 record doesn't outrank a well-established one.
      This is a <strong>team-level</strong> result, not a claim that these two
      Pokémon fought each other.
    </p>
    <div class="damage-result" id="matchup-h2h-headline"></div>
    <h4>Matchup profile</h4>
    <p class="sub">Each side's overall record across every decided match its teams played, and its single best and worst opponent — both chosen by Wilson lower bound over a minimum sample, so a 1&#8209;0 record never reads as a best matchup.</p>
    <div class="matchup-picker-grid" id="matchup-summary"></div>
    <h4>Defender's toughest opponents</h4>
    <p class="sub">Pokémon whose teams beat the defender's teams most reliably (minimum 10 recorded matches).</p>
    <div class="grid-6xn" id="matchup-h2h-grid"></div>

    <h3>Co-usage</h3>
    <p class="sub">Pokémon most often teamed with the defender in real tournament rosters. This is a teammate-pairing view, not a matchup signal — the head-to-head section above is the matchup signal.</p>
    <div class="grid-6xn" id="matchup-co-usage-grid"></div>
  </section>

