    <div class="subtab-panel" data-subpanel="ds-caveats" hidden>
      <p class="sub">
        Standing limitations that apply to figures elsewhere on this
        dashboard. Each is a property of what the sources publish, not a bug
        to be fixed here.
      </p>
      <ul class="caveat-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Head-to-head is team vs team, never Pokémon vs Pokémon.</strong>
          No source publishes a per-battle log naming which four of six were
          actually brought, so a "matchup" figure means teams containing A
          beat teams containing B — it is attributed to the whole roster.
          The one Pokémon-vs-Pokémon figure on the site is a profile's
          Checks and counters, which comes from Showdown ladder battle logs,
          not tournaments.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Matchup appearance counts overstate sample roughly 6×</strong>
          for the same reason: every pairing is counted against all six
          Pokémon on each side.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The legal pool is an upper bound.</strong> PokéBase
          publishes no removal signal, so the cumulative legal-Pokémon count
          can only grow — a later-banned Pokémon is never subtracted.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Signature share is structurally capped at 16.7%</strong> —
          a Pokémon can appear only once on a six-slot team — which is why
          players are ranked by share of their <em>teams</em> instead.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Everything here is Champions-format only.</strong> The
          tournament corpus also covers standard VGC events; every usage and
          win-rate figure is filtered to Champions events first. Blending the
          two would be comparing different games.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Tournament data has no Stat Point spreads.</strong>
          Official team sheets publish ability, held item, Stat Alignment
          (nature) and moves and nothing more. The damage calculator
          therefore assumes a fully invested level-50 baseline on both
          sides (32 Stat Points, IVs fixed at 31) rather than any real
          spread. A profile's Spreads panel shows what Showdown ladder
          players ran, a different population; no tournament view uses it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The Showdown ladder is its own population.</strong>
          Smogon's monthly statistics count every rated ladder battle, weighted
          toward 1760+ players. They sit beside tournament figures in the
          Usage tab's Ladder view and the profile's Counters and Spreads, are
          labelled there, and are never added to a tournament figure.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Legality has a single snapshot date</strong>, so nothing on
          this dashboard trends legality over time; usage trends are measured
          across tournament dates instead.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Champions stat deltas are all zero.</strong> No rebalance
          has been published yet, so every Pokémon's Champions stats still
          equal its canonical stats.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
